// Ch15 B05 "After", B06 "The shoal", B07 "The confession" and B08 "Still below" (C/E, ~9 min).
// act2_ch15.md §2 B05-B08. THE REVEAL, mandated (SPEC §3.5), by Kerrid's own word, at sea, among friends.
// RULE 1: nobody performs a rite on him, nobody attacks, nobody exposes him; he tells them before anyone asks.
// RULE 2: every mote is HELD and moves SIDEWAYS: the shoal's dead toward him, his own leaving his hands from
// the rope-burns (≤ 0.6). Nothing rises; nothing turns gold (his light lifts only at H09).
// RULE 4: the facts are exact (ADR 0022 + sweeps): he KEPT THE GATE and opened it for Imra every dawn and
// dusk, never walked beside her; he HELD DACE'S LINE at the rings for eight low tides, and they did not drink
// together; Imra and Dace never met before the stair; she went down for a diver she had never met; he does
// NOT know what became of Dace; no rank, no title, no promise.
// RULE 5: Kerrid's one long speech (voice guide). Short blocks, broken by the others. `kerrid_at_sea` is a
// bed for a voice: it never swells under a line, and drops out for two bars on "Your father, Rhen."
// The camera never stands over him: every shot of him is at his seated eye height or below.
title: ch15_the_shoal
location: ch15/open_sea
---
@letterbox on
@camera U07
@music unlamped fade=1.0
@anim asha sleep_sitting
@wait 4.0
@camera K01
@music silence fade=3.0
@vfx glimmer_held at=shoal_floor count=48 rate=slow
@wait 3.0
@camera K02
@vfx glimmer_held at=shoal_rising count=36 rate=slow
@wait 3.0
@camera K03
@vfx glimmer_held at=kerrid_orbit count=18 rate=slow
@wait 3.0
@camera K04
@music kerrid_at_sea fade=4.0
@vfx glimmer_held at=kerrid_scar count=6 rate=slow
@wait 3.0
@anim asha wake
@anim rhen wake
@wait 1.5
<<jump ch15_the_confession>>
===
// B07, K05 onward. Kerrid SITS DOWN on the deck by the bier: the first time anyone has seen him sit. He
// rests his forearms on his knees and holds his hands still, palms up; the motes leaving them slow. The
// party gathers without being asked: Asha nearest, Rhen opposite, Toma standing, Ysolde, Liss by the bier
// with her hand on the cloth, Pell at the rail with his back to the water. Nobody reaches for him.
title: ch15_the_confession
---
@camera K05
@anim kerrid sit_down
@sfx kerrid_sits
@wait 3.0
@mark asha kerrid_near walk
@mark rhen kerrid_opposite walk
@mark toma kerrid_standing walk
@mark ysolde kerrid_ysolde walk
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [neutral]: I'll tell it before you ask. You've been very patient. #line:ch15_conf_001
@camera K06
Kerrid [neutral]: I kept the Fisher Stair at Corrow. Fourteen years. Captain of the watch. #line:ch15_conf_002
Kerrid [neutral]: Fishers, all of us. No rank. The wall's the Order's. The stair's ours. #line:ch15_conf_003
@camera K07
@anim kerrid look_at asha
Kerrid [neutral]: Eleven years ago a Cantor came for the Coilspire trial. The path to the headland goes out through my gate. #line:ch15_conf_004
Kerrid [soft_smile]: I opened it for her every dawn. Every dusk. We said good morning. She laughed at the wrong times. #line:ch15_conf_005
@camera K08
@anim kerrid look_at rhen
Kerrid [neutral]: Same eight days I'd hired a Low Reaches lamp-diver. To re-seat the rings at the stair foot, under low water. #line:ch15_conf_006
Kerrid [neutral]: I held his line. Eight low tides. He slouched. #line:ch15_conf_007
@camera K09
Kerrid [neutral]: They never met. She was a Cantor with a Stillguard escort. He was a wright with his marks under his sleeves. #line:ch15_conf_008
Kerrid [neutral]: I was the only man in Corrow who knew them both. #line:ch15_conf_009
@camera K10
Kerrid [sad]: On the eighth day the sea went out and came back early. He was under the stair foot at the last ring. #line:ch15_conf_010
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [grief]: She heard a man drowning under my stair and went down for him. A diver she'd never met. Your father, Rhen. #line:ch15_conf_011 #tn:"The first time Kerrid uses Rhen's name in the game. It should land hard."
@camera K11
@wait 3.5
@camera K12
Kerrid [sad]: I held the gate past the hour. Went down after them. Got them both on the stair. #line:ch15_conf_012
Kerrid [tender]: She hummed to the children going up ahead of her. Kept them climbing. #line:ch15_conf_013
@camera K13
@anim kerrid turn_palms
Kerrid [neutral]: I was last on the hand-line when the sea came over. It ran through my hands. #line:ch15_conf_014
@wait 1.5
Kerrid [determined]: I held it. #line:ch15_conf_015
@camera K14
@face kerrid guilty
Kerrid [guilty]: Your father reached back for me. He missed. I don't think he forgave himself. #line:ch15_conf_016
@wait 2.0
@camera K15
Kerrid [neutral]: I woke at the next low tide, at the foot of the stair, with the drowned. Corrow had already lit my name. #line:ch15_conf_017
Kerrid [neutral]: I'd stood on the wall twice while they Stilled one of us. I was gone before light. #line:ch15_conf_018 #tn:"'Stilled': the Order's rite on the dead who stay (the Stilling). It is mentioned, never shown."
@camera K16
@anim kerrid look_at asha
Kerrid [grief]: I got your mother up the stair. That's all I did. I got her up so she could walk to the Choir. #line:ch15_conf_019
@camera K17
@anim asha touch comb
@wait 1.5
@anim asha look_at rhen_lantern
Asha [grief]: A man with a lantern like that brought me this. I was seven. #line:ch15_conf_020 #tn:"'This' is the tortoiseshell comb in her hair. 'A lantern like that': Rhen's lantern's twin."
@anim rhen look_at rhen_lantern
@wait 2.5
@camera K18
Toma [neutral]: Your breath. In Ullar. #line:ch15_conf_021
Kerrid [neutral]: Yes. #line:ch15_conf_022
<<if $ch08_fishwife_called>>
    @wait 2.0
    Toma [sad]: The watch at Corrow tells it every Rising. The captain who held the stair. I served seven years on that wall and never knew his face. #line:ch15_conf_023 #long
    Kerrid [neutral]: Nobody did. That was the point of a watch. #line:ch15_conf_024
<<endif>>
<<if $ch05_heard_straw_cape_tale>>
    Rhen [sad]: The big man in the straw cape. The one who pulls them out. #line:ch15_conf_025
    Kerrid [neutral]: Somebody has to. #line:ch15_conf_026
<<endif>>
<<if $ch08_fishwife_called>>
    Kerrid [sad]: Marra knew me. On the stair. I went down a step so she'd stop looking. #line:ch15_conf_027
<<endif>>
<<if $ch13_sat_at_moorings>>
    Kerrid [soft_smile]: You stood at the moorings with me. You didn't ask. I noticed. #line:ch15_conf_028
<<endif>>
<<if $ch14_steps_held>>
    Kerrid [neutral]: Held a stair again. At a wedding. Didn't expect that. #line:ch15_conf_029
<<endif>>
@wait 2.0
Rhen [grief]: What happened to him? After? #line:ch15_conf_030
Kerrid [sad]: I don't know. I was in no state to ask. #line:ch15_conf_031 #tn:"Dry, not a joke: he had just drowned."
@anim kerrid look_at sea_south
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [neutral]: She walked on to the Choir. A captain doesn't come off the wall while there's anyone below. #line:ch15_conf_032
<<set $ch15_kerrid_told = true>>
<<jump ch15_still_below>>
===
// B08 "Still below" (E, 1.5 min). K19: nobody moves to do anything to him. Asha sits down beside him, not as
// a Cantor, as a person, shoulder to shoulder; she does NOT touch his hands. The motes leaving them slow and
// stop (the scar eases to Ch10's faint leak over ~6 s); the shoal's motes drift on past the barge and sink
// back, still held, still sideways. Then each of them, briefly; Kerrid last, opening his Act III voice.
// No "Be level" from Toma (it's gone).
title: ch15_still_below
---
@camera K19
@mark asha kerrid_beside walk
@anim asha sit_beside kerrid
@wait 6.0
@anim liss look_at pell
Liss [angry]: You knew? #line:ch15_below_001
Pell [neutral]: From the first day. It was his to say. #line:ch15_below_002
<<set $ch15_pell_said_he_knew = true>>
Ysolde [tender]: Thank you for telling us, Kerrid. #line:ch15_below_003
@anim toma nod kerrid
@wait 1.5
Rhen [sad]: You knew who I was. In Pemakar. #line:ch15_below_004
Kerrid [neutral]: Yes. #line:ch15_below_005
Rhen [sad]: You could've said. #line:ch15_below_006
Kerrid [guilty]: You'd have asked me the end. I didn't have it. #line:ch15_below_007
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [soft_smile]: I have nothing left to hide. I may as well talk. #line:ch15_below_008
@camera K20
@music silence fade=6.0
@wait 6.0
@fade out 3.0
@letterbox off
===
